# Icons

## Style

- Lucide-compatible stroke icons, 24×24 grid, `stroke-width: 2`,
  `currentColor`, monocolor. Always through the `Icon` wrapper
  (`design-system/icons/Icon.tsx`), sizes `sm/md/lg`.

## The rule

> Play'Up uses an icon when it **encodes a state or a repeated object family
> that speeds up scanning** (navigation destinations, row statuses, D9
> attention rows, icon-only chrome actions, meta facts like date/time/venue),
> but **not** when it would decorate a unique label already carried by
> typography (text buttons, one-off titles, prose).

## Where icons belong

- Rail destinations (always icon + label).
- Panel heads: optional small neutral icon **only** for recurring content
  families (Équipes, Règlement, Calendrier, Classement).
- À traiter rows (part of the D9 recipe).
- Match Hero meta band (calendar / clock / pin).
- Trend and live indicators.

## Where icons are forbidden

- Inside standings/table cells (except trend column).
- On text buttons ("Saisir le résultat" needs no pencil).
- Repeated per-row decorations (no ball icon on every match row).
- Emojis, filled icon sets, multicolor icons: never.
